<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nyungu ya Mawe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1884</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nyungu ya Mawe was a Nyamwezi warlord of the 19th century in what is now western Tanzania. A member of the ruling house of Unyanyembe, he broke with his kin and the Arab traders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabora">Tabora</a> in the 1860s and from around 1870 used bands of ruga-ruga to conquer the Kimbu chiefdoms to the south. He ruled through appointed officials rather than hereditary chiefs, creating an unusually centralised state.</p></div>
